# AutoFish — Profile Authoring Conventions

## Schema
Profiles conform to `contracts/fishing-profile.schema.json` (JSON Schema draft 2020-12, `additionalProperties: false`).

## Required Fields
Every profile must have: `id`, `displayName`, `zoneName`, `targetSkill`, `enabledSkills`, `pacing`, `thresholds`, `guardrails`.

## Rules
- **`id`:** lowercase + hyphens only (`^[a-z0-9-]+$`). Must be unique across all profiles.
- **`enabledSkills`:** at least 1 entry. Typical values: `fishing`, `survival`, `cooking`.
- **`pacing.reactionCeilingMs`** must be >= `reactionFloorMs`.
- **All threshold values** must be non-negative integers.
- **`notes`:** keep short and operational. Operator-facing guidance only.
- **`guardrails`:** all three booleans required (`pauseOnCombat`, `pauseOnBridgeLoss`, `recoverOnDrift`).

## Pacing → Proof Command Mapping
- `pacing.biteTimeoutMs` → `--cast-wait-seconds` default.
- `pacing.lootTimeoutMs` → `--post-pull-delay-ms` default.
- CLI overrides always take precedence over profile defaults.

## Validation
```powershell
.\scripts\validate-profiles.ps1
```
Run this after any profile change. It checks schema compliance, id uniqueness, and value constraints.

## Python Helper Usage
```powershell
# By profile id (looks up profiles/ directory)
python tools\autofish-helper-py\autofish_helper.py signal-proof one-cast --profile starter-pond --dry-run

# By JSON path (for testing new profiles before committing)
python tools\autofish-helper-py\autofish_helper.py signal-proof one-cast --profile profiles\my-new-profile.json --dry-run
```
The selected profile and applied defaults are written into the proof manifest.
